'''Reginald Leon Evans''' (born January 5, 1959) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[running back]] for the [[Washington Redskins]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL). He played [[college football]] for the [[Richmond Spiders football|Richmond Spiders]]. He is now coaching in Reston for the Reston Seahawks youth football program.

Evans is the current board chairman of the Fellowship of Christian Athletes for [[Loudoun County, Virginia]] and uses his influence as a former professional athlete to help younger athletes make the right choices in their lives as athletes, young men and women, and as followers of Christ. He also spends time mentoring coaches through his experiences and through life experiences of others.

Evans attended [[York High School (Yorktown, Virginia)|York High School]] in [[Yorktown, Virginia]] where he played [[high school football|football]], [[basketball]] and [[track and field]].  He became a Scholastic High School All-American.  Besides being All-District in all three sports, he was voted to participate in the Virginia High School All-Star game in football.  In track & field, he won a state title in the Long Jump his senior year.
